  "description": "NEJZOU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H76 Dy5 N56 Ni8 O24 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),2(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1,10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni4A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.419-4.174 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.08-127.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C83H106Dy5Ni8N61O44. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
